  "notes": [
    "Recorded by W1 follow-up 1 (task_label W1-followup-1); the task field is left out because run@1 accepts only W<n>-S<nn> or W<n>-T<nn> there.",
    "Each configuration ran in its own fresh server: docker run -d of postgres:18@sha256:74935e72241653ca55e0414067e6d8763aceb8a810eb51b452253ec3dcfc4336 with --network none, --memory=6g and trust authentication, the work directory mounted read-only at /q; the recorder waited until docker logs showed \"PostgreSQL init process complete\" and \"database system is ready to accept connections\" twice and pg_isready exited 0 (at most 120 polls, 0.5 s apart), then ran psql through docker exec and sh with stdout and stderr merged by 2>&1, so the log is in the order psql wrote it, and removed the container. argv lists the commands in order (start, prelude when there is one, psql, removal); started_at, duration_s and exit_code are the psql command's. psql ran with -X and -v VERBOSITY=verbose, so each ERROR line carries its SQLSTATE; the SQL files ran unchanged, several -f files in one psql session.",
    "values.partition is S6.L1 cell 2's first SELECT: p, NOT p and p IS NULL each count one of the three rows. values.eq_null_rows is the row count of `WHERE bal = NULL` and values.is_null_ids the ids of `WHERE bal IS NULL`. values.null_amount_update is the command tag of the guarded UPDATE with a NULL amount. values.check_only_overdraft is S6.L2 cell 2: the UPDATE fails with 23514 (\"new row for relation \\\"acct\\\" violates check constraint \\\"acct_bal_check\\\"\") and the balance stays 50.",
    "The s06-statements configuration is the recorder's: it is not a lesson cell, and states each keyed statement as a query whose result psql printed. Its RETURNING old.bal, new.bal is the reference plan's s1 with $from = 2 and $amt = 30 over a balance of 50 (old 50, new 20, UPDATE 1), then the same statement with $amt = 80, whose guard matches nothing (0 rows, UPDATE 0); psql headed both columns `bal`.",
    "Spine section 9.5 and curriculum/S06-correspondence.md line 490 name 18.6 and PGlite; PGlite was not run for this record, which holds PostgreSQL 18.6 only. Placeholder in argv: <sandbox>/work is a scratch copy of the inputs this record lists, mounted at /q."
